    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-142718: sum the probabilities for Y=-1 and Y=1 to obtain 0.2+0.45=0.65. q-142575: Y<2 means Y=1, whose column totals 5/7. q-6812: at t=0, x'=-1 and y'=2, so dy/dx=-2. q-20990: y'/x'=(2t+2)/(2e^t(t+1))=e^{-t}, giving 1/e at t=1. q-6808: at t=π/6, x'=-2 and y'=3, giving slope -3/2. q-70965 and q-70968: use the given point as the position vector and the two independent given vectors as plane directions. q-33819: the cross product is (-33,13,-41), perpendicular to both plane directions. q-70972: the cross product is (-5,3,1), also perpendicular to both directions. q-128501 and q-128499: use the specified point and the direction vectors of the two lines. q-71036: Q-P=(-1,-15,-2) and R-P=(0,-6,-1) are independent plane directions. q-128741: Q-P=(2,-2,-1) and R-P=(3,5,-1) are independent plane directions. q-126740: the point corresponds to t=2, where r'=(-1,-2,1). q-75199: r'(0)=(1,-1,0). q-126841: r(0)=(0,1) and r'(0)=(0,-5), so the tangent is (0,1)+u(0,-5) for every real u. No prior submitted answer or grade was supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematical verification.",
